-- title:
--   Partial Atkin–Lehner automorphism w_Q for squarefree Q coprime to N
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $Q$ be natural numbers with $Q$ nonzero, $Q$ squarefree and $\gcd(N,Q)=1$. Write $j_q \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant and, for $e \ge 1$, let $j_q(q^e)$ denote its image under the ring homomorphism `qExpand` $\mathbb{Q}\, e$ of Laurent series induced by multiplying the exponents by $e$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull` $(NQ)$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all $j_q(q^e)$ with $e$ a nonzero divisor of $NQ$. The assertion is that there exists a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F$ such that for every nonzero $d$ dividing $N$ one has $\sigma(j_q(q^{d})) = j_q(q^{dQ})$ and $\sigma(j_q(q^{dQ})) = j_q(q^{d})$, the two elements being taken in $F$ via the divisibility relations $d \mid NQ$ and $dQ \mid NQ$. Only existence is claimed: no uniqueness, no statement that $\sigma$ is an involution, and no prescription of the values of $\sigma$ on the remaining generators $j_q(q^{dQ'})$ with $Q' \mid Q$, $1 < Q' < Q$.
--
--   This is the existence of the partial Atkin–Lehner automorphism $w_Q$ on the function field of $X_0(NQ)$, in the concrete model of that field as the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^e)$, $e \mid NQ$. It is obtained from the prime-level case [`ModularCurve.exists_isAtkinLehnerAutFull_of_prime_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isAtkinLehnerAutFull_of_prime_of_not_dvd) and is used in the analysis of Hecke divisors on the modular curves occurring later in the argument.
